      "id": "authentication.gateway-modes",
      "parent_category": "authentication",
      "priority": "required",
      "question": "How do integrated OAuth, external OIDC, and externally managed authentication change gateway behavior?",
      "reason": "The GatewayConfig CR drives authentication mode selection. When Spec.OIDC is set, the kube-auth-proxy uses the specified OIDC issuer URL via oauth2-proxy. K8s service account token validation is enabled by default (EnableK8sTokenValidation). External OIDC providers are supported through ProviderCASecretName and VerifyProviderCertificate fields. The proxy passes authorization headers to upstream, operates with TLS termination using configurable min version and cipher suites, and supports TokenReview rate limiting.",
      "remaining_question": ""
    },
