      "id": "compliance.runtime-fips",
      "parent_category": "fips_compliance",
      "priority": "required",
      "question": "Which build or packaging signals exist, and what source evidence establishes or limits runtime FIPS claims?",
      "reason": "Manager binary built with CGO_ENABLED=1, GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime, -tags rhoai on UBI9-minimal-pqc base (OpenSSL present). Cloudmanager uses -tags strictfipsruntime but CGO_ENABLED is parameterized via build arg rather than hardcoded. Application-level TLS uses crypto/tls with OpenShift APIServer TLS profile. FIPS limitation documented for cloudmanager's conditional CGO_ENABLED and unverified kube-auth-proxy image.",
      "remaining_question": ""
